data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_0def61174fb94f30016ac952e246a08196b0e49fb24afb82e4","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing server-rendered forms**\n\nI'm considering how to create simple server-rendered forms without needing JavaScript, just using HTML, CSS, and a JavaScript server. I think about the endpoints, like POST for /projects, which would handle redirects and errors by rendering a 400 status with an alert for the role. I'll use a row div with a heading for the open button and a GET request to direct the user. SQLite prepared orders for the ID should be effective. It seems like I have enough time to verify everything with tests in a temporary server setup."},"sequence_number":111,"summary_index":0}

